  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree with NNN nodes, where the ithi^{th}ith node has a value AiA_iAi​ associated to it.\n\nYou need to answer QQQ queries. Each query is of the form:\n\n\nXXX YYY : Given two nodes XXX and YYY (1≤X,Y≤N)(1\\le X,Y\\le N)(1≤X,Y≤N), find the length of the **longest** arithmetic progression formed using the values of nodes on the shortest path between XXX and YYY.\n\nMore formally, let there be MMM nodes on the shortest path between nodes XXX and YYY, and GGG denote the shortest path from node XXX to node YYY, where G1=XG_1 = XG1​=X, GM=YG_M = YGM​=Y, and there exists an edge between nodes GiG_iGi​ and Gi+1G_{i+1}Gi+1​ for all (1≤i&lt;M)(1 \\leq i &lt; M)(1≤i&lt;M).\n\nLet BBB denote the array [AG1,AG2,…,AGM][A_{G_1} , A_{G_2}, \\dots, A_{G_M}][AG1​​,AG2​​,…,AGM​​]. Find the length of the **longest** subarray of BBB which is an **arithmetic progression**.\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer NNN, denoting the number of nodes in the tree.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1,A_2,\\ldots,A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​, the values assigned to each node.\nNext N−1N-1N−1 lines contains 222 space-separated integers uuu and vvv denoting edge between nodes uuu and vvv.\nNext line contains QQQ, the number of queries.\nNext QQQ lines contain 222 space-separated integers XXX and YYY.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each query, print the length of the **longest** arithmetic progression formed using the values of nodes on the shortest path between XXX and YYY.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N,Q≤2⋅1051 \\leq N,Q \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N,Q≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
