        "input": "10\n1 3 6 3 5 4 5 4 6 4\n1 2\n2 3\n1 4\n4 5\n6 3\n7 3\n8 5\n9 5\n10 7\n5\n9 10\n6 5\n8 4\n7 2\n6 8",
        "output": "3\n3\n2\n2\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe tree looks like:\n\nQuery 111: The shortest path between nodes 999 and 101010 is [9,5,4,1,2,3,7,10][9,5,4,1,2,3,7,10][9,5,4,1,2,3,7,10]. The corresponding array B=[A9,A5,A4,A1,A2,A3,A7,A10]=[6,5,3,1,3,6,5,4]B = [A_9, A_5, A_4, A_1, A_2, A_3, A_7, A_{10}] = [6, 5, 3, 1, 3, 6, 5, 4]B=[A9​,A5​,A4​,A1​,A2​,A3​,A7​,A10​]=[6,5,3,1,3,6,5,4].\nThe longest subarray of BBB which is also an arithmetic progression are [5,3,1][5, 3, 1][5,3,1] and [6,5,4][6, 5, 4][6,5,4].\nThus, the length of the longest subarray is 333.\nQuery 222: The shortest path between nodes 666 and 555 is [6,3,2,1,4,5][6, 3, 2, 1, 4, 5][6,3,2,1,4,5]. The corresponding array B=[A6,A3,A2,A1,A4,A5]=[4,6,3,1,3,5]B = [A_6, A_3, A_2, A_1, A_4, A_5] = [4, 6, 3, 1, 3, 5]B=[A6​,A3​,A2​,A1​,A4​,A5​]=[4,6,3,1,3,5].\nThe longest subarray of BBB which is also an arithmetic progression is [1,3,5][1, 3, 5][1,3,5].\nThus, the length of the longest subarray is 333."
